{"type": "tool_call", "n": 19, "ts": 1790155558.7513878, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2013 Q1 2026 US Software Subscriptions (GL 6200): board deck vs. ledger\n\nPrepared by: David Murguia, 2026-04-03. No entries posted.\n\n1. Deck figure\nBoard deck Appendix B (DOC-0207), prepared by FP&A from the GL as of 2026-04-01 09:00, reports Q1 2026 US Software Subscriptions (GL 6200) of USD 11,769.00.\n\n2. Ledger today\nGL 6200, US entity, period activity:\n  Jan 2026   4,289.70\n  Feb 2026   4,139.80\n  Mar 2026   6,139.50\n  Q1 total  14,569.00\nDifference vs. deck: USD 2,800.00.\n\n3. What explains the difference (exactly)\nOne entry: JE-00304, dated 2026-03-31, Dr 6200 / Cr 2000 USD 2,800.00, memo \"Tessellate BI - TB-Q1-TRUEUP - Q1 seat true-up\", source AP, posted by ap.clerk, created 2026-04-02 10:14 \u2014 i.e. ~25 hours after the deck snapshot was taken. Removing JE-00304 from March gives 3,339.50, and Q1 becomes 4,289.70 + 4,139.80 + 3,339.50 = 11,769.00, tying to the deck to the cent. No other 6200 entry in Jan\u2013Mar was added, changed, or reversed after the snapshot.\n\n4. Is JE-00304 correctly in Q1?\nYes. Support DOC-0206 (Tessellate BI invoice TB-Q1-TRUEUP, dated 2026-03-31) describes \"Q1 2026 seat true-up (14 additional seats, Jan\u2013Mar)\", USD 2,800.00. Service period is entirely within Q1, so recognizing the full amount in March 2026 is correct under accrual accounting. The entry is supported and requires no correction. It is also a distinct charge from the three monthly Tessellate invoices already in 6200 (TES-19846, TES-37216, TES-55710 at 1,950.00 each), not a duplicate.\n\n5. Correct Q1 figure\nUSD 14,569.00. The deck is stale, not the ledger. Logged EXC-001 recommending FP&A refresh Appendix B; the underlying issue is that AP posted a March-dated invoice after FP&A pulled the deck.\n\n6. Other observation (not part of the variance)\nGL 6200 has two Zoom card entries on 2026-03-08 (JE-00247, JE-00248, 149.90 each). I checked whether this was a ledger duplicate: the March bank statement shows two separate Zoom debits that day (BT-US-0062, BT-US-0063) and each JE has its own receipt (DOC-0173, DOC-0174), so the ledger agrees with cash. Whether Zoom double-billed is a vendor/cardholder question, not a GL error, and it was already in the ledger before the deck snapshot, so it does not affect the reconciliation above. No action taken.\n\nComposition of the Q1 14,569.00 for reference: Tessellate BI monthly 3 \u00d7 1,950.00 = 5,850.00; Tessellate Q1 true-up 2,800.00; Quire Docs monthly 3 \u00d7 640.00 = 1,920.00; Figtree prepaid license amortization 2 \u00d7 1,250.00 = 2,500.00 (Jan, Feb only \u2014 no March amortization entry is present, which the close owner for prepaid software should confirm is intentional); Zoom card charges 10 \u00d7 149.90 = 1,499.00. Total 14,569.00."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
